1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:02,154
If you press the button in front of you,

2
00:00:02,154 --> 00:00:04,080
you'll win $50,000.

3
00:00:04,100 --> 00:00:05,920
But someone you don't know will die.

4
00:00:06,190 --> 00:00:07,570
You won't see who it is.

5
00:00:07,790 --> 00:00:09,290
You won't even learn their name.

6
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:10,963
Would you press it?

7
00:00:10,963 --> 00:00:13,403
Richard Matheson's story "Button, Button,"

8
00:00:13,403 --> 00:00:14,306
published in 1970,

9
00:00:14,306 --> 00:00:16,280
puts you face to face with exactly

10
00:00:16,280 --> 00:00:17,593
this kind of offer.

11
00:00:18,293 --> 00:00:19,648
A package is left at the door

12
00:00:19,648 --> 00:00:20,863
of Norma and Arthur,

13
00:00:20,863 --> 00:00:21,883
who live in New York.

14
00:00:22,403 --> 00:00:24,563
Inside is a small wooden box.

15
00:00:24,963 --> 00:00:25,920
On top of the box,

16
00:00:25,920 --> 00:00:27,513
under a locked glass cover,

17
00:00:27,513 --> 00:00:28,863
there's a single button.

18
00:00:29,583 --> 00:00:31,421
The note next to it says a Mr. Steward

19
00:00:31,421 --> 00:00:32,813
will come by at 8 p.m.

20
00:00:33,773 --> 00:00:34,893
When Steward arrives,

21
00:00:34,893 --> 00:00:36,456
he leaves the key on the table

22
00:00:36,456 --> 00:00:37,863
and explains his offer.

23
00:00:38,093 --> 00:00:39,583
If they press the button,

24
00:00:39,583 --> 00:00:41,883
they'll get $50,000.

25
00:00:41,883 --> 00:00:43,343
And somewhere in the world,

26
00:00:43,343 --> 00:00:45,787
a person they don't know will die.

27
00:00:45,787 --> 00:00:47,807
But who he works for, he won't say.

28
00:00:48,177 --> 00:00:49,539
Arthur ends the conversation,

29
00:00:49,539 --> 00:00:50,467
sends the man away,

30
00:00:50,467 --> 00:00:52,437
and tears up the card he left behind.

31
00:00:52,967 --> 00:00:54,611
But Norma can't stop thinking

32
00:00:54,611 --> 00:00:55,807
about the box.

33
00:00:55,807 --> 00:00:56,474
The next day,

34
00:00:56,474 --> 00:00:58,304
she pieces the card back together

35
00:00:58,304 --> 00:00:59,397
and calls Steward.

36
00:00:59,627 --> 00:01:00,980
The man repeats that they won't

37
00:01:00,980 --> 00:01:02,137
know the person who dies,

38
00:01:02,137 --> 00:01:04,037
and they won't see them die.

39
00:01:04,517 --> 00:01:05,180
That evening,

40
00:01:05,180 --> 00:01:07,247
the package shows up at their door again.

41
00:01:07,317 --> 00:01:08,844
Norma takes the box and hides it

42
00:01:08,844 --> 00:01:09,760
in the cabinet.

43
00:01:09,760 --> 00:01:10,300
At dinner,

44
00:01:10,300 --> 00:01:11,597
she brings it up.

45
00:01:11,597 --> 00:01:13,567
What if the offer is real?

46
00:01:13,567 --> 00:01:14,160
For Arthur,

47
00:01:14,160 --> 00:01:15,447
the answer doesn't change.

48
00:01:15,497 --> 00:01:17,061
Not knowing the victim won't change

49
00:01:17,061 --> 00:01:18,157
what they'd be doing.

50
00:01:19,097 --> 00:01:19,633
Norma, though,

51
00:01:19,633 --> 00:01:20,800
thinks about everything

52
00:01:20,800 --> 00:01:22,079
she's put off for years:

53
00:01:22,079 --> 00:01:23,807
the trip to Europe,

54
00:01:23,807 --> 00:01:25,457
the little house on the island,

55
00:01:25,457 --> 00:01:27,753
the chance of having a child someday.

56
00:01:27,753 --> 00:01:28,526
The next morning,

57
00:01:28,526 --> 00:01:29,866
once Arthur leaves for work,

58
00:01:29,866 --> 00:01:31,247
she takes out the box.

59
00:01:31,247 --> 00:01:32,530
She opens the glass cover

60
00:01:32,530 --> 00:01:33,937
and presses the button.

61
00:01:33,937 --> 00:01:34,997
Nothing happens.

62
00:01:35,277 --> 00:01:36,756
Norma decides it's all nonsense

63
00:01:36,756 --> 00:01:38,557
and throws the box in the trash.

64
00:01:38,937 --> 00:01:39,812
But that evening,

65
00:01:39,812 --> 00:01:41,477
a call comes from a hospital.

66
00:01:41,887 --> 00:01:43,475
In the crowd on a subway platform,

67
00:01:43,475 --> 00:01:46,277
Arthur was pushed in front of a train,

68
00:01:46,277 --> 00:01:47,740
and he lost his life.

69
00:01:47,740 --> 00:01:49,010
In that moment,

70
00:01:49,010 --> 00:01:51,337
Norma remembers the insurance.

71
00:01:51,337 --> 00:01:54,925
Her husband's $25,000 life insurance pays

72
00:01:54,925 --> 00:01:57,071
double for accidental death:

73
00:01:57,071 --> 00:01:59,210
exactly $50,000.

74
00:01:59,210 --> 00:02:00,943
She pulls the box out of the trash

75
00:02:00,943 --> 00:02:02,137
and breaks it open.

76
00:02:02,137 --> 00:02:03,645
There are no wires inside,

77
00:02:03,645 --> 00:02:04,854
and no mechanism.

78
00:02:04,854 --> 00:02:07,377
The box is completely empty.

79
00:02:07,377 --> 00:02:08,911
The phone rings again.

80
00:02:08,911 --> 00:02:10,170
It's Steward.

81
00:02:10,170 --> 00:02:12,025
Norma screams that they told her she

82
00:02:12,025 --> 00:02:13,930
wouldn't know the person who'd die.

83
00:02:13,930 --> 00:02:15,826
Steward asks her whether she ever

84
00:02:15,826 --> 00:02:17,350
really knew her husband.

85
00:02:18,050 --> 00:02:18,900
For Norma,

86
00:02:18,900 --> 00:02:20,137
the person who would pay

87
00:02:20,137 --> 00:02:21,380
the price was a distant,

88
00:02:21,380 --> 00:02:22,990
nameless stranger.

89
00:02:22,990 --> 00:02:24,842
But every stranger was someone

90
00:02:24,842 --> 00:02:27,040
else's nearest and dearest.

